{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979372-what-does-it-mean-to-walk-a-path-interpretations","id":979372,"title":"What does it mean to walk a Path? Interpretations.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-30T17:59:51-07:00","id":979372,"title":"What does it mean to walk a Path? Interpretations.","content":"So, I've had this sitting in the back of my head for a while now and I've decided that it's good enough as a first draft to share publicly.<br /> <br /> Basically, I find the Path descriptions in the book to be a bit too flowery and poetic and not quite clear enough at actually conveying the core ideas of each Path and what makes each distinct from the others. In a lot of the discussions I've had online, I've found that a lot of people struggle with what it means to belong to each Path beyond the mechanical advantages afforded. This is my attempt to rewrite that stuff in a way that's more coherent and usable.<br /> <br /> I wanted something that was a straightforward explanation to be paired with different Realms and Arcana so that you could have independent interpretations of those things from their stereotypical Path, and also a vehicle with which you could think about why an Arcanum was Inferior for that Path, but nevertheless still entirely valid as a strong option if that's how you build your character. Basically, I wanted Paths to be able to stand on their own enough that, like the Orders, you could port them to another system if that's what you wanted to do.<br /> ---<br /> <br /> Acanthus<br /> The Acanthus is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>agency</b>. Everyone lives a scripted life, walking through the motions as actors on a stage. That\u2019s the story that the world tells, and you\u2019re just a face in that crowd, looking busy, lacking meaning. The Acanthus take control of the narrative, and thereby power over their life and the consequent world around them. They diverge from the script and say, \u201cYes, I can. And I will <i>because </i>I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mastigos<br /> The Mastigos is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>relationships</b>. Everyone lies to each other, putting up outward facades while their inner life is in turmoil. They turn away from each other and themselves, refusing to acknowledge necessary truths, poisoning their community. The Mastigos say that, \u201cDistance is a Lie.\u201d They forcibly create bridges where there were walls, and relish in the growing pains that come with having to come face-to-face with both others and oneself.<br /> <br /> Moros<br /> The Moros is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>components</b>. Everyone has a fixed notion of what constitutes an object, that lead is lead and gold is gold, that a child is a child and a man is a man. They go through their lives trying to acquire new things, ignoring that they could patch together everything they need from what they already have. The Moros breaks free of this attitude, reducing complexities into simple construction blocks and rebuilding them into something greater than the original arrangements. They watch and guide the transition from youth to age, from desolation to creation, from past to future.<br /> <br /> Obrimos<br /> The Obrimos is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>keystones</b>. Everyone presumes that things are disparate and disconnected, that you can manipulate one thing without affecting anything else. That\u2019s what it looks like on the outside: the superficial facade that people see everyday. The Obrimos understands that beneath such illusions is the hard truth of energy cycling through systems underlying the reality. They find the key that binds a thousand worlds together and turn it, opening a thousand locks at once and freeing a thousand minds with a single word, \u201cSee.\u201d<br /> <br /> Thyrsus<br /> The Thyrsus is a Mage who looks at the world through the eyes of <b>negotiations</b>. Everyone sees an inanimate world, a terra nullius uncultivated and ripe for the taking. They can\u2019t see that something was already there, something that deserves consideration and comprehension. The Thyrsus hears these indigenous voices, speaks on their behalf, and answers them in return. The worlds are full of their own peoples, and those peoples must be accounted for when you endeavor their lands in your own right. It doesn\u2019t matter that a world might be within a person, or beyond a veil.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> I think that I'd like to add more sections per Path, and clean up the language a bunch, but I felt like this much was enough to share for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}